<title>SINGAPORE: Malaysia sets Nov crude term premium at 75 cents.</title>
<headline>Malaysia sets Nov crude term premium at 75 cents.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia has set its November premium for term lifting crude at 75 cents per barrel, up from 55 cents in October, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said they expected Petronas, the state oil company, to set its retrospective term lifting prices for its various crudes sometime next week, including its benchmark Tapis grade.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
